## Simulated integrations and authored examples

- data/examples/synthetic_profiles.json: three handcrafted fictional companies.
- data/examples/synthetic_news.json: one handcrafted fictional news item.
- llm/agent/contracts/insight.example.json: handwritten contract example, not LLM output.
- llm/agent/model_policy.json: proposed routing/budget configuration, not an
  implemented gateway.
- API paths and orchestrator in the report: architecture proposals only.
- frontend/src/data/: fictional companies, news items and bank-analytics quotes for the UI demo.
  All of it is marked as synthetic in the interface. Bank quotes there are invented
  illustrations, not text from the supplied PDFs. The only real text is the 11 September 2026
  key-rate example taken from the case brief.
- frontend/src/components/Illustrations.tsx: original SVG illustrations drawn by the team;
  no bank artwork is copied.
- frontend/src/components/Brand.tsx and frontend/public/favicon.svg: the Alfa-Bank "A" mark path is taken from the
  open-source package @alfalab/icons-logotype (icon AlfaBankLIcon, MIT licence, Alfa-Bank design system); the mark is a
  trademark of Alfa-Bank and is used here for a demonstration prototype built for the organiser. The red tile around it,
  the demo company logos and the "Cabinet" home screen art are the team's own simplified imitations drawn in the style
  of the organisers' screenshots; no other official bank logo files, brand assets or brand book were used.
- frontend/src/api/mock/: in-browser mock of the backend used when VITE_API_MODE=mock.
- The demo login, the manager message / request / callback buttons and the browser
  notifications in the frontend simulate bank integrations (authorisation, CRM,
  push channel). Nothing is sent outside the browser.
- The online-banking home screen, accounts and payments in the frontend are a mock-up of the
  bank interface, not an integration.

No live news feed, bank API, LLM provider, production bank interface or real
counterparty identity resolution has been connected. No external system was
used as the core runtime of the proposed hackathon solution.

The analysis/code preparation was assisted by the chat coding assistant.
The assistant's internal model/deployment identifier is not available as a
project dependency and is not claimed to be one of the allowed runtime LLMs.
It is not wired into the resulting scripts or proposed application.

## Development-only tools

The shell, Debian package download/extraction utilities and the environment's
web search were used during preparation. One public search attempted to
identify the initially unspecified SIGMA reference; no matching reference was
established from that search. The user subsequently supplied a SIGMA description,
which informed the architecture plan. No SIGMA
source code or LangChain runtime was imported. No external news dataset was
downloaded by that search.

License texts for Apache-2.0 and GPL-2 are retained under licenses.
Before release, append every newly added library, image/container, model,
embedding service, news provider and dataset with exact version and terms.

